<h2 id="deal">The Gibbs Deal</h2>
<p>Jahmyr Gibbs and the Detroit Lions agreed Thursday, August 6 on a three-year extension worth $67.5 million, with a maximum value of $75.75 million and $51.5 million guaranteed. The $22.5 million annual average makes Gibbs the highest-paid running back in NFL history — surpassing the mark Bijan Robinson had set with the Atlanta Falcons just two days earlier. The deal runs through the 2030 season and officially ended Gibbs's hold-in, which began when he reported to camp but sat out the Lions' first six practices of the summer.</p>
