<h2 id="week">A Wild Week for RB Contracts</h2>
<p>What makes this moment remarkable isn't just Gibbs's number — it's how fast the running back market moved. In the span of a single week, three different backs reset what the position could earn:</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Player</th><th>Team</th><th>Contract</th><th>Annual Average</th></tr>
<tr><td>Jahmyr Gibbs</td><td>Lions</td><td>3 yrs, $67.5M ($75.75M max)</td><td>$22.5M</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bijan Robinson</td><td>Falcons</td><td>3 yrs, $66.75M ($75M max)</td><td>$22.25M</td></tr>
<tr><td>Jonathan Taylor</td><td>Colts</td><td>2 yrs, $44M</td><td>$22.0M</td></tr>
<tr><td>Saquon Barkley (2025)</td><td>Eagles</td><td>2 yrs, $41.2M</td><td>$20.6M</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Robinson, Gibbs, and Taylor now form a new "$20 million club" alongside Barkley, who became the first back to cross that threshold last year after his 2,000-yard, Super Bowl-winning season. Four running backs now earn at least $20 million annually — a number that didn't exist in the position's contract history before this offseason.</p>
<div class="callout">
<strong>Why It Happened So Fast</strong>
  Robinson and Gibbs were both 2023 first-round picks entering the final guaranteed years of their rookie deals, and both held in at camp while their reps negotiated separately — each reportedly reluctant to sign first and set a number the other could easily top. Once Robinson signed on August 4, Gibbs's camp had a clear target to beat, and did so within 48 hours.
</div>
<h2 id="production">Why Gibbs Earned It</h2>
<p>Gibbs's production over his first three NFL seasons is statistically unmatched. His 49 career touchdowns through three seasons are the most in NFL history for a player at that stage of his career, surpassing the previous record of 47 held by Lions legend Barry Sanders. He's also first in the league in scrimmage yards (3,768) and scrimmage touchdowns (38) over the past two seasons, and is only the second player in NFL history — after Nick Chubb — to average at least 5.0 yards per carry in each of his first three seasons.</p>
