<p>For the full breakdown of Gibbs's 2023 combine profile against Robinson's — including the 4.36 forty and 33.5-inch vertical that made evaluators grade him as an elite athletic talent even at 199 pounds — see our <a class="inline" href="https://athletecalculator.com/bijan-robinson-jahmyr-gibbs-contract-holdout-athletic-profile">Robinson vs. Gibbs athletic comparison</a>.</p>
<h2 id="next">What's Next</h2>
<p>With Gibbs back at practice in a limited capacity as of Thursday, the Lions now shift focus to a backfield without David Montgomery, who is no longer Gibbs's primary running mate after his own extension expired. Gibbs enters 2026 firmly in the conversation for fantasy football's overall RB1, and the question league-wide now becomes whether any other back — Christian McCaffrey, Derrick Henry, or a rising name like Bijan Robinson himself — can push the market even higher before next offseason.</p>
<h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Who is the highest-paid running back in the NFL right now?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Jahmyr Gibbs, at $22.5 million per year on his new three-year extension with the Detroit Lions, signed August 6, 2026.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">How long did Bijan Robinson hold the highest-paid RB record?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Just two days. Robinson signed his extension with the Falcons on August 4, and Gibbs surpassed it on August 6.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Why did three running backs get record contracts in the same week?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Robinson and Gibbs were both entering the final year of their rookie deals as 2023 first-round picks and had been holding in at camp during negotiations. Jonathan Taylor's deal came the same day as Gibbs's, largely because his representatives had also been negotiating against the same rising market. Once one back signed, it created urgency and a new benchmark for the others.</div>
</div>
